settings-performance-power-card = Laptop & power
settings-performance-power-card-desc = The picker stops rendering when it settles. Wallpaper renderers keep running after it closes, so they have separate battery limits.
settings-performance-power-source-label = Current power source
settings-performance-power-battery-limited = Battery (automatic limits are active)
settings-performance-power-battery-unlimited = Battery (automatic limits are disabled)
settings-performance-power-external = External power, desktop, or unavailable (automatic limits are inactive)
settings-performance-battery-saver-label = Automatic battery saver
settings-performance-battery-saver-desc = Apply the FPS and video-idle limits below while the battery is discharging. Power changes are picked up automatically.
settings-performance-gpu-label = Picker GPU
settings-performance-gpu-desc = Auto prefers a low-power GPU while the battery saver is active. Low power asks for an integrated GPU, High performance a discrete one. Reopen the picker after changing this. WGPU_POWER_PREF wins.
settings-performance-gpu-auto = Auto (recommended)
settings-performance-gpu-low = Low power
settings-performance-gpu-high = High performance
settings-performance-gpu-none = Driver default
settings-performance-battery-fps-label = On-battery picker FPS
settings-performance-battery-fps-desc = Cap picker animation while discharging. The normal Max FPS still applies if lower; 0 disables this cap.
settings-performance-battery-idle-label = On-battery video idle pause
settings-performance-battery-idle-desc = Pause video rendering, decode, and audio after this many idle seconds while discharging. The shorter of this and the Paper idle pause wins; 0 disables it.
settings-performance-battery-wallpaper-label = Wallpaper performance mode on battery
settings-performance-battery-wallpaper-desc = While discharging, use direct NV12 video, hard cuts, and a 30 fps, 2048 px limit for native scenes. Less detail, much less work per frame.
settings-performance-rendering-card = Active rendering
settings-performance-rendering-card-desc = Every active frame redraws the full window, so a lower cap cuts GPU and compositor work. The picker still drops to 0 FPS when settled.
settings-performance-we-renderer-label = Wallpaper Engine scene renderer
settings-performance-we-renderer-value = Built-in Vulkan
settings-performance-max-fps-label = Max FPS
settings-performance-max-fps-desc = Normal animation frame-rate cap. Set it to the display refresh rate for maximum smoothness, or 60 for a cooler laptop.
settings-performance-preview-fps-label = Transition preview FPS
settings-performance-preview-fps-desc = Limit the transition preview in Motion settings. Every preview frame redraws the whole picker.
settings-performance-hover-previews-label = Hover video previews
settings-performance-hover-previews-desc = Decode and animate video thumbnails while you interact. They pause when idle; off uses the least power.
settings-performance-image-opt-card = Image optimisation
settings-performance-image-opt-card-desc = Replace PNG, JPEG, and single-frame GIF wallpapers with smaller validated WebP files. Animated GIFs and Workshop assets are never touched; originals stay recoverable.
settings-performance-auto-optimize-label = Auto-optimise new images
settings-performance-auto-optimize-desc = Check new images as they arrive. An image is replaced only when the WebP passes the quality floor and saves enough space.
settings-performance-quality-label = Quality
settings-performance-quality-desc = Light: q82, 30 dB floor, 15% minimum savings. Balanced: q88, 32 dB, 10%. Quality: pixel-lossless WebP, 5%.
settings-performance-quality-light = Light
settings-performance-quality-balanced = Balanced
settings-performance-quality-quality = Quality
settings-performance-resolution-label = Max resolution
settings-performance-resolution-desc = Images above the cap are downscaled. Smaller images are never upscaled.
settings-performance-optimize-all-label = Optimise all images
settings-performance-optimize-all-desc = Run image optimisation across the wallpaper library.
settings-performance-optimize-action = Optimise
settings-performance-trash-card = Trash
settings-performance-trash-card-desc = After a replacement is validated, the original moves to hidden recovery storage on the same filesystem until it is deleted for good.
settings-performance-retention-label = Image retention
settings-performance-retention-desc = Days to keep trashed images before auto-cleanup.
settings-performance-retention-unit = days
settings-performance-auto-delete-label = Auto-delete images after retention
settings-performance-auto-delete-desc = Permanently delete trashed images once they exceed the retention period.
settings-performance-thumbs-card = Thumbnails & cache
settings-performance-thumb-jobs-label = Max concurrent thumbnail jobs
settings-performance-thumb-jobs-desc = Number of thumbnail jobs that run in parallel during cache rebuilds.
settings-performance-clear-cache-label = Clear all cached data
settings-performance-clear-cache-desc = Erase all cached thumbnails and regenerate from scratch on next scan.
settings-performance-clear-cache-action = Clear
settings-performance-recompute-label = Recompute colours
settings-performance-recompute-desc = Re-derive per-wallpaper colour bucket and saturation from existing thumbnails.
settings-performance-recompute-action = Recompute
settings-performance-diagnostics-card = Diagnostics
settings-performance-diagnostics-card-desc = Check the environment for problems that stop wallpapers applying. Full detail goes to the log and `skwd-walld --doctor`.
settings-performance-doctor-label = Run diagnostics
settings-performance-doctor-desc = Run environment checks and summarise any issues.
settings-performance-doctor-action = Run
settings-performance-bug-report-label = Generate bug report
settings-performance-bug-report-desc = Bundle version, environment, diagnostics, and recent logs into one file to attach to an issue.
settings-performance-bug-report-action = Generate

settings-performance-device-label = Wallpaper GPU
settings-performance-device-desc = Choose the GPU for native wallpaper rendering. An unavailable card falls back to Automatic. Plasma shared images use Plasma's own GPU.
settings-performance-device-auto = Automatic
settings-performance-device-unavailable = Saved GPU unavailable (using Automatic)

settings-performance-capture-we-label = Add captured frame thumbnails to all WE wallpapers
settings-performance-capture-we-desc = Capture native scenes in the background. Reuse valid captures and keep existing previews if a scene fails. You can stop and continue later.
settings-performance-capture-we-action = Generate thumbnails
settings-performance-capture-we-stop = Stop
